Bridge-backed harnesses such as Claude Code and Codex require using real network sandbox
like @ai-sdk/sandbox-vercel. Host-runtime harnesses such as Pi can also run with
@ai-sdk/sandbox-just-bash because they do not need a sandbox-exposed port.

With Output.json(), the AI SDK only checks that the response is valid JSON;
it doesn't validate the structure or types of the values. If you need schema
validation, use Output.object() or Output.array() instead.

@ai-sdk/tui provides a terminal UI for running
AI SDK agents locally. It is designed for ToolLoopAgent instances that can run
from free-form terminal input.

Cursor runs inside the sandbox through @ai-sdk/harness-acp. It requires a
